winners give up all the time never give  up is bad advice real winners won't  hesitate to walk away from an  unsuccessful venture master the art of  moving on by learning when to quit and  when to keep going have you heard the  one about the athlete who faces obstacle  after obstacle refuses to give up and  finally overcomes the odds in the end to  win the gold it makes her a great movie  but in reality most people who aspire to  become professional athletes fail  it's simple math really for someone to  win many others have to lose fortunately  when it comes to finding the work you  were born to do you don't usually have  to compete against thousands of other  people and if something isn't working  you don't need to keep going in fact you  probably should real winners give up all  the time many people who try and try  again only to come short of a big  victory never really recover sometimes  even the ones who do make it struggle  later with any kind of meaningful second  act the real secret is that selective  quitting is a powerful practice you just  need to learn when to give up and when  they keep going you may be familiar with  this old adage often attributed to  Albert Einstein the definition of  insanity is doing the same thing over  and over and expecting different results  Einstein was right in that the real  danger of going insane or just failing  over and over doesn't usually come from  doing something new rather the worst  failures come from doing something that  we've been doing for a while most of us  are smart enough to realize that if we  try something new  doesn't work we can't just keep doing  the same thing and expect different  results we might try it once more but  we'll usually switch up the tactic even  mice and a maze will learn to adapt an  attempt different solution if they hit  the same dead end enough times when the  stakes are low make changes or give up  quickly don't waste time on small things  and when the stakes are low make changes  right away fight your fear of missing  out while fear of missing out is a very  normal and natural human emotion it can  be dangerous if it prevents you from  quitting when it's long past time to  give up after all if you want to be  successful you can't live your life out  of fear ignore sunk costs as much as  possible it doesn't matter how much  you've invested in something whether  time money or any other resource next  time you're at the grocery store and a  better line opens up take it use the  answers to two questions that guide your  decisions ask yourself these two basic  questions 1 is it working - do you still  enjoy it you don't need to overthink  these questions and you shouldn't  sugarcoat the answers you'll be far more  successful in the long term if you're  honest with yourself about each of them  contrary to popular belief if you want  to win you shouldn't always just keep  going you should regroup and try  something totally different winners  never quit and quitters never win is  alive to win sometimes you need to find  a new game to play  winners give up all the time  [Music]
 

